  "body": "Found by mkinney's QA runs (p02, p03, p04, p05, p08) and reproduced on a minimal part by a separate verification run on 2026-11-18, CamCraft main `83867fd7` (= v0.24.0 code). Minimal repro projects and posted programs are kept on mkinney's machines and can be attached.\n\nWhat happens: every new operation is seeded `feed: 1200, plunge_feed: 300` whatever the tool's own feed, even with the stock material set (`set_stock_material aluminium_6061`). Posted:\n```\nG73 X0 Y0 Z-12.803 R0 Q18 F300        (DR-0600, tool feed 115 -> 2.6x)\nG73 X0 Y0 Z-13.043 R0 Q20.4 F300      (custom DR-0680, tool feed 200 -> 1.5x)\nG3 X1.077 Y0 Z-9.687 I0.538 J0 F317   (TM-0600-P125 thread mill: 1200 mm/min at the cutting edge, tool feed 400 -> 3x)\n```\n`suggest_cutting_data` / `apply_cutting_data` refuse both kinds, so the user has no supported way to get a tool-based feed for them. Nothing warns.\n\nWhy P1: wrong posted feeds, up to 3x the tool's rating on a small thread mill and 2.6x on a 6 mm drill, post silently - a broken tool in the part.\n\nDone means: drill, peck and thread-mill operations take their feed from the tool (or the cutting-data table for the stock material) when created; a feed above the tool's rating is refused or warned by name; pinned by a test that posts these three ops and reads the F words.\n",
